FT                   /note="Domain:cl26462:FhuF_C FhuF 2Fe-2S C-terminal domain.
FT                   Members of this protein family, including FhuF of E. coli,
FT                   are siderophore ferric iron reductases that appear to play
FT                   a role in iron removal from certain hydroxamate-type
FT                   siderophores, including coprogen, ferrichrome, ferrioxamine
FT                   B, and aerobactin. Genes occur in regularly in siderophore
FT                   transport and/or biosynthesis clusters. The C-terminus
FT                   includes four Cys residues in a C-C-10(X)-C-X-X-C motif
FT                   that binds a 2Fe-2S cluster. Family TIGR03950 is similar,
FT                   but especially in the C-terminal region, but likely acts on
FT                   a different panel of siderophores. [Energy metabolism,
FT                   Electron transport, Transport and binding proteins, Cations
