FT                   /note="Domain:cl21461:Globin_like Globin-like proteins.
FT                   This family includes protoglobin from Methanosarcina
FT                   acetivorans C2A. It is also found near the N-terminus of
FT                   the Haem-based aerotactic transducer HemAT in Bacillus
FT                   subtilis. It is part of the haemoglobin superfamily.
FT                   Protoglobin has specific loops and an amino-terminal
FT                   extension which leads to the burying of the haem within the
FT                   matrix of the protein. Protoglobin-specific apolar tunnels
FT                   allow the access of O2, CO and NO to the haem distal site.
FT                   In HemAT it acts as an oxygen sensor domain. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:25-132, Eval:5.8e-09, score:48.5]"
