FT                   /note="Domain:cl27087:SPOR Sporulation related domain. FtsN
FT                   is a poorly conserved protein active in cell division in a
FT                   number of Proteobacteria. The N-terminal 30 residue region
FT                   tends to by Lys/Arg-rich, and is followed by a
FT                   membrane-spanning region. This is followed by an acidic
FT                   low-complexity region of variable length and a
FT                   well-conserved C-terminal domain of two tandem regions
FT                   matched by pfam05036 (Sporulation related repeat), found in
FT                   several cell division and sporulation proteins. The role of
FT                   FtsN as a suppressor for other cell division mutations is
FT                   poorly understood; it may involve cell wall hydrolysis.
FT                   [Cellular processes, Cell division] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:212-321, Eval:1.0e-06, score:46.0, N-term missing]"
