FT                   /note="Domain:cl26870:CobW_C Cobalamin synthesis protein
FT                   cobW C-terminal domain. The family of proteins identified
FT                   by this model is generally found proximal to the trimeric
FT                   cobaltochelatase subunit CobN which is essential for
FT                   vitamin B12 (cobalamin) biosynthesis. The protein contains
FT                   an P-loop nucleotide-binding loop in the N-terminal domain
FT                   and a histidine-rich region in the C-terminal portion
FT                   suggesting a role in metal binding, possibly as an
FT                   intermediary between the cobalt transport and chelation
FT                   systems. A broader CobW family is delineated by two Pfam
FT                   models which identify the N- and C-terminal domains
FT                   (pfam02492 and pfam07683). [Biosynthesis of cofactors,
FT                   prosthetic groups, and carriers, Heme, porphyrin, and
FT                   cobalamin] [Superfamily, Aligned:5-286, Eval:2.6e-47,
