FT                   /note="Domain:cl14632:VOC vicinal oxygen chelate (VOC)
FT                   family. Toxoflavin lyase (TflA) is metalloenzyme degrading 
FT                   toxoflavin at the presence of  oxygen, Mn(II), and
FT                   dithiothreitol. TflA is structurally homologous to proteins
FT                   of the vicinal oxygen chelate superfamily. The structure of
FT                   TflA contains  fold that displays a rare rearrangement of
FT                   the structural modules indicative of domain permutation.
FT                   Moreover, unlike the 2-His-1-carboxylate facial triad
FT                   commonly utilized by vicinal oxygen chelate dioxygenases
FT                   and other dioxygen-activating non-heme Fe(II) enzymes, the
FT                   metal center in TflA consists of a 1-His-2-carboxylate
FT                   facial triad. Toxoflavin  is an azapteridine that is toxic
FT                   to various plants, fungi, animals, and bacteria.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:1-141, Eval:5.3e-73, score:212.0]"
FT                   /note="MGA_1789"
