FT                   /note="Domain:cl28318:PulE Type II secretory pathway ATPase
FT                   GspE/PulE or T4P pilus assembly pathway ATPase PilB [Cell
FT                   motility, Intracellular trafficking, secretion, and
FT                   vesicular transport, Extracellular structures]. This model
FT                   describes a protein of type IV pilus biogenesis designated
FT                   PilB in Pseudomonas aeruginosa but PilF in Neisseria
FT                   gonorrhoeae; the more common usage, reflected here, is
FT                   PilB. This protein is an ATPase involved in protein export
FT                   for pilin assembly and is closely related to GspE
FT                   (TIGR02533) of type II secretion, also called the main
FT                   terminal branch of the general secretion pathway. Note that
FT                   type IV pilus systems are often divided into type IV-A and
FT                   IV-B, with the latter group including bundle-forming pilus,
FT                   mannose-sensitive hemagglutinin, etc. Members of this
FT                   family are found in type IV-A systems. [Cell envelope,
FT                   Surface structures, Protein fate, Protein and peptide
FT                   secretion and trafficking] [Superfamily, Aligned:1-355,
FT                   Eval:0.0e+00, score:504.7]"
