FT                   /note="Domain:cl27723:Orn_DAP_Arg_deC Pyridoxal-dependent
FT                   decarboxylase, C-terminal sheet domain. Two alternative
FT                   pathways can convert arginine to putrescine. One is
FT                   decarboxylation by this enzyme followed by removal of the
FT                   urea moeity by agmatinase. In the other, the ureohydrolase
FT                   (arginase) acts first, followed by ornithine decarboxylase.
FT                   This pathway leads to spermidine biosynthesis, hence the
FT                   gene symbol speA. A distinct biodegradative form is also
FT                   pyridoxal phosphate-dependent but is not similar in
FT                   sequence. [Central intermediary metabolism, Polyamine
FT                   biosynthesis] [Superfamily, Aligned:26-389, Eval:2.8e-81,
FT                   score:252.2]"
