FT                   Eval:0.0e+00]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl27616:PQQ PQQ enzyme repeat. Members of
FT                   this family closely resemble quinoproteins and
FT                   quinohemoproteins such as PQQ-dependent methanol, glucose,
FT                   and shikimate dehydrogenases, but restricted to species of
FT                   Acidobacteria unable to synthesize PQQ. Seven members occur
FT                   in candidatus Solibacter usitatus Ellin6076, eleven in
FT                   Acidobacteriaceae bacterium KBS 96, etc. Members have
FT                   N-terminal signal sequences. They lack the pair of adjacent
FT                   Cys residues, involved in electron transfer, typical for
FT                   family TIGR03075, and they lack CxxCH motifs for cytochrome
FT                   c-like heme-binding. What cofactor these paralogous
FT                   families of enzymes might use is unclear. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:21-785, Eval:0.0e+00, score:703.1]"
