FT                   /note="Domain:cl27726:Secretin Bacterial type II and III
FT                   secretion system protein. Several related protein families
FT                   encode outer membrane pore proteins for type II secretion,
FT                   type III secretion, and type IV pilus formation. This
FT                   protein family appears to encode a secretin for pilus
FT                   formation, although it is quite different from PilQ.
FT                   Members include the PilN lipoprotein of the plasmid R64
FT                   thin pilus, a type IV pilus. Scoring between the trusted
FT                   and noise cutoffs are examples of bundle-forming pilus B
FT                   (bfpB). [Cell envelope, Surface structures, Protein fate,
FT                   Protein and peptide secretion and trafficking]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:36-199, Eval:1.6e-14, score:68.6,
FT                   C-term missing]"
