FT                   /note="Domain:cl28529:COG4277 Predicted DNA-binding protein
FT                   with the Helix-hairpin-helix motif  [General function
FT                   prediction only]. This uncharacterized protein of about 400
FT                   amino acids in length contains a radical SAM protein in the
FT                   N-terminal half. Members are present in about twenty
FT                   percent of prokaryotic genomes, always paired with a member
FT                   of the conserved hypothetical protein TIGR03915. Roughly
FT                   forty percent of the members of that family exist as
FT                   fusions with a uracil-DNA glycosylase-like region,
FT                   TIGR03914. In DNA, uracil results from deamidation of
FT                   cytosine, forming U/G mismatches that lead to mutation, and
FT                   so uracil-DNA glycosylase is a DNA repair enzyme. This
FT                   indirect connection, and the recurring role or radical SAM
FT                   protein in modification chemistries, suggest that this
FT                   protein may act in DNA modification, repair, or both.
FT                   [Unknown function, Enzymes of unknown specificity]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:1-404, Eval:0.0e+00, score:536.3]"
