FT                   /note="Domain:cl28413:HisS Histidyl-tRNA synthetase
FT                   [Translation, ribosomal structure and biogenesis]. This
FT                   model finds a histidyl-tRNA synthetase in every completed
FT                   genome. Apparent second copies from Bacillus subtilis,
FT                   Synechocystis sp., and Aquifex aeolicus are slightly
FT                   shorter, more closely related to each other than to other
FT                   hisS proteins, and actually serve as regulatory subunits
FT                   for an enzyme of histidine biosynthesis. They were excluded
FT                   from the seed alignment and score much lower than do single
FT                   copy histidyl-tRNA synthetases of other genomes not
FT                   included in the seed alignment. These putative second
FT                   copies of HisS score below the trusted cutoff. The
FT                   regulatory protein kinase GCN2 of Saccharomyces cerevisiae
FT                   (YDR283c), and related proteins from other species
FT                   designated eIF-2 alpha kinase, have a domain closely
FT                   related to histidyl-tRNA synthetase that may serve to
FT                   detect and respond to uncharged tRNA(his), an indicator of
FT                   amino acid starvation; these regulatory proteins are not
FT                   orthologous and so score below the noise cutoff. [Protein
FT                   synthesis, tRNA aminoacylation] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:15-192, Eval:6.7e-25, score:97.3, C-term missing]"
