FT                   /note="Domain:cl26247:DNA_pol3_delta2 DNA polymerase III,
FT                   delta subunit. This model represents the well-conserved
FT                   first ~ 365 amino acids of the translation of the dnaX
FT                   gene. The full-length product of the dnaX gene in the model
FT                   bacterium E. coli is the DNA polymerase III tau subunit. A
FT                   translational frameshift leads to early termination and a
FT                   truncated protein subunit gamma, about 1/3 shorter than tau
FT                   and present in roughly equal amounts. This frameshift
FT                   mechanism is not necessarily universal for species with DNA
FT                   polymerase III but appears conserved in the exterme
FT                   thermophile Thermus thermophilis. [DNA metabolism, DNA
FT                   replication, recombination, and repair] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:22-157, Eval:4.9e-26, score:105.2, C-term missing]"
