FT                   /note="Domain:cl27046:CopB Copper resistance protein B
FT                   precursor (CopB). This family consists of several bacterial
FT                   copper resistance proteins. Copper is essential and serves
FT                   as cofactor for more than 30 enzymes yet a surplus of
FT                   copper is toxic and leads to radical formation and
FT                   oxidation of biomolecules. Therefore, copper homeostasis is
FT                   a key requisite for every organism. CopB serves to extrude
FT                   copper when it approaches toxic levels. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:26-287, Eval:1.5e-103, score:302.2, N-term
FT                   missing]"
