FT                   /note="Domain:cl00504:Cytochrom_C_asm Cytochrome C assembly
FT                   protein. Members of this protein family represent one of
FT                   two essential proteins of system II for c-type cytochrome
FT                   biogenesis. Additional proteins tend to be part of the
FT                   system but can be replaced by chemical reductants such as
FT                   dithiothreitol. This protein is designated CcsB in
FT                   Bordetella pertussis and some other bacteria, resC in
FT                   Bacillus (where there is additional N-terminal sequence),
FT                   and CcsA in chloroplast. We use the CcsB designation here.
FT                   Member sequences show regions of strong sequence
FT                   conservation and variable-length, poorly conserved regions
FT                   in between; sparsely filled columns were removed from the
FT                   seed alignment prior to model construction. [Energy
FT                   metabolism, Electron transport, Protein fate, Protein
FT                   modification and repair] [Superfamily, Aligned:23-270,
FT                   Eval:5.3e-72, score:219.1]"
FT                   /note="MGA_2594"
