FT                   /note="Domain:cl14648:Aldose_epim aldose 1-epimerase
FT                   superfamily. Members of this protein family act as
FT                   galactose mutarotase (D-galactose 1-epimerase) and
FT                   participate in the Leloir pathway for galactose/glucose
FT                   interconversion. All members of the seed alignment for this
FT                   model are found in gene clusters with other enzymes of the
FT                   Leloir pathway. This enzyme family belongs to the aldose
FT                   1-epimerase family, described by pfam01263. However, the
FT                   enzyme described as aldose 1-epimerase itself (EC 5.1.3.3)
FT                   is called broadly specific for D-glucose, L-arabinose,
FT                   D-xylose, D-galactose, maltose and lactose. The restricted
FT                   genome context for genes in this family suggests members
FT                   should act primarily on D-galactose. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:11-290, Eval:6.8e-74, score:225.7]"
