FT                   /note="Domain:cl27534:COG2907 Predicted NAD/FAD-binding
FT                   protein  [General function prediction only]. The sequences
FT                   in this family are members of the pfam01593 superfamily of
FT                   flavin-containing amine oxidases which include the phytoene
FT                   desaturases. These sequences also include a FAD-dependent
FT                   oxidoreductase domain, pfam01266. The genes of the family
FT                   modeled here are generally in the same locus with genes
FT                   involved in the biosynthesis and elaboration of squalene,
FT                   the condensation product of the polyisoprenoid farnesyl
FT                   pyrophosphate. This gene and its association with hopene
FT                   biosynthesis in Zymomonas mobilis has been noted in the
FT                   literature where the gene symbol hpnE was assigned. This
FT                   gene is also found in contexts where the downstream
FT                   conversion of squalene to hopenes is not evidence. The
FT                   precise nature of the reaction catalyzed by this enzyme is
FT                   unknown at this time. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-415,
FT                   Eval:1.0e-175, score:495.5]"
