FT                   /note="Domain:cl27024:PlcC Phospholipase C  [Cell
FT                   wall/membrane/envelope biogenesis]. Members of this protein
FT                   family are bacterial, phosphatidylcholine-hydrolyzing
FT                   phospholipase C enzymes, with a characteristic domain
FT                   architecture as found in hemolytyic (PlcH) and nonhemolytic
FT                   (PlcN) secreted enzymes of Pseudomonas aeruginosa. PlcH
FT                   hydrolyzes phosphatidylcholine to diacylglycerol and
FT                   phosphocholine, but unlike PlcN can also hydrolyze
FT                   sphingomyelin to ceramide ((N-acylsphingosine)) and
FT                   phosphocholine. Members of this family share the
FT                   twin-arginine signal sequence for Sec-independent transport
FT                   across the plasma membrane. PlcH is secreted as a
FT                   heterodimer with a small chaperone, PlcR, encoded
FT                   immediately downstream. [Cellular processes, Pathogenesis]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:15-560, Eval:4.7e-99, score:307.8]"
