FT                   /note="Domain:cl27253:Allantoicase Allantoicase repeat.
FT                   Members of this family are the enzyme allantoicase (EC
FT                   3.5.3.4), also called allantoate amidinohydrolase. This
FT                   enzyme hydrolyzes allantoate to (S)-ureidoglycolate and
FT                   urea; it can also degrade (R)-ureidoglycolate to glyoxylate
FT                   and urea. Allantoinase (EC 3.5.2.5) hydrolyzes
FT                   (S)-allantoin (a xanthine metabolite, via urate) to
FT                   allantoate. Allantoate can then be degraded either by this
FT                   enzyme, allantoicase, or by allantoate deiminase (EC
FT                   3.5.3.9). Members of the seed alignment for this model were
FT                   taken from BRENDA. Proteins in this family contain two
FT                   copies of the allantoicase repeat (pfam03561). A different
FT                   but similarly named enzyme, allantoate amidohydrolase (EC
FT                   3.5.3.9), simultaneously breaks down the urea to ammonia
FT                   and carbon dioxide. [Purines, pyrimidines, nucleosides, and
FT                   nucleotides, Other, Energy metabolism, Other] [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:8-328, Eval:0.0e+00, score:519.3]"
