FT                   /note="Domain:cl26335:RbgA Ribosome biogenesis GTPase A
FT                   [Translation, ribosomal structure and biogenesis]. Members
FT                   of this protein family are GTP-binding proteins involved in
FT                   ribosome biogenesis, including the essential YlqF protein
FT                   of Bacillus subtilis, which is an essential protein. They
FT                   are related to Era, EngA, and other GTPases of ribosome
FT                   biogenesis, but are circularly permuted. This family is not
FT                   universal, and is not present in Escherichia coli, and so
FT                   is not as well studied as some other GTPases. This model is
FT                   built for bacterial members. [Protein synthesis, Other]
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:6-69, Eval:2.1e-08, score:52.8,
FT                   C-term missing]"
FT                   /note="Domain:cl26333:FeoB_N Ferrous iron transport protein
FT                   B. This model describes the family of the [Fe] hydrogenase
FT                   maturation protein HypF as characterized in Chlamydomonas
FT                   reinhardtii and found, in an operon with radical SAM
FT                   proteins HydE and HydG, in numerous bacteria. It has GTPase
FT                   activity, can bind an 4Fe-4S cluster, and is essential for
FT                   hydrogenase activity. [Protein fate, Protein modification
FT                   and repair] [Superfamily, Aligned:4-166, Eval:1.6e-07,
FT                   score:49.9, C-term missing]"
