FT                   intracellular modules that pair together to form a stable
FT                   globular domain. This family represents a single CBS
FT                   domain. Pairs of these domains have been termed a Bateman
FT                   domain. CBS domains have been shown to bind ligands with an
FT                   adenosyl group such as AMP, ATP and S-AdoMet. CBS domains
FT                   are found attached to a wide range of other protein domains
FT                   suggesting that CBS domains may play a regulatory role
FT                   making proteins sensitive to adenosyl carrying ligands. The
FT                   region containing the CBS domains in Cystathionine-beta
FT                   synthase is involved in regulation by S-AdoMet. CBS domain
FT                   pairs from AMPK bind AMP or ATP. The CBS domains from IMPDH
FT                   and the chloride channel CLC2 bind ATP. [Superfamily,
FT                   Aligned:35-655, Eval:6.9e-135, score:406.4]"
FT                   /note="MGA_3730"
