FT                   /note="Domain:cl28576:COG3435 Gentisate 1,2-dioxygenase 
FT                   [Secondary metabolites biosynthesis, transport and
FT                   catabolism]. This family consists of gentisate
FT                   1,2-dioxygenases. This ring-opening enzyme acts in
FT                   salicylate degradation that goes via gentisate rather than
FT                   via catechol. It converts gentisate to maleylpyruvate. Some
FT                   putative gentisate 1,2-dioxygenases are excluded by a
FT                   relatively high trusted cutoff score because they are too
FT                   closely related to known examples of 1-hydroxy-2-naphthoate
FT                   dioxygenase. Therefore some homologs may be bona fide
FT                   gentisate 1,2-dioxygenases even if they score below the
FT                   given cutoffs. [Superfamily, Aligned:2-56, Eval:7.3e-09,
FT                   score:46.3, N-term missing]"
