FT                   /note="Domain:cl28154:FlgG Flagellar basal body rod protein
FT                   FlgG [Cell motility]. This model encompasses three closely
FT                   related flagellar proteins usually denoted FlgE, FlgF and
FT                   FlgG. The names have often been mis-assigned, however.
FT                   Three equivalog models, TIGR02489, TIGR02490 and TIGR02488,
FT                   respectively, separate the individual forms into three
FT                   genome-context consistent groups. The major differences
FT                   between these genes are architectural, with variable
FT                   central sections between relatively conserved N- and
FT                   C-terminal domains. More distantly related are two other
FT                   flagellar apparatus familis, FlgC (TIGR01395) which
FT                   consists of little else but the N-and C-terminal domains
FT                   and FlgK (TIGR02492) with a substantial but different
FT                   central domain. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-244, Eval:2.3e-113,
FT                   score:322.9]"
FT                   /note="MGA_3969"
