FT                   /note="Domain:cl00282:cbb3_Oxidase_CcoQ N/A. This family
FT                   consists of several Cbb3-type cytochrome oxidase components
FT                   (FixQ/CcoQ). FixQ is found in nitrogen fixing bacteria.
FT                   Since nitrogen fixation is an energy-consuming process,
FT                   effective symbioses depend on operation of a respiratory
FT                   chain with a high affinity for O2, closely coupled to ATP
FT                   production. This requirement is fulfilled by a special
FT                   three-subunit terminal oxidase (cytochrome terminal oxidase
FT                   cbb3), which was first identified in Bradyrhizobium
FT                   japonicum as the product of the fixNOQP operon.
FT                   [Superfamily, Aligned:1-47, Eval:1.5e-08, score:43.1]"
