FT                   This family consists of bacterial antibiotic resistance
FT                   proteins, which confer resistance to various
FT                   aminoglycosides they include: aminoglycoside
FT                   3'-phosphotransferase or kanamycin kinase /
FT                   neomycin-kanamycin phosphotransferase and streptomycin
FT                   3''-kinase or streptomycin 3''-phosphotransferase. The
FT                   aminoglycoside phosphotransferases inactivate
FT                   aminoglycoside antibiotics via phosphorylation. This family
FT                   also includes homoserine kinase. This family is related to
FT                   fructosamine kinase pfam03881. [Superfamily,
