FT                   /note="Domain:cl00755:zf-dskA_traR Prokaryotic dksA/traR
FT                   C4-type zinc finger. Members of this predicted regulatory
FT                   protein are found only in endospore-forming members of the
FT                   Firmicutes group of bacteria, and in nearly every such
FT                   species; Clostridium perfringens seems to be an exception.
FT                   The member from Bacillus subtilis, the model system for the
FT                   study of the sporulation program, has been designated both
FT                   yteA and yzwB. Some (but not all) members of this family
FT                   show a strong sequence match to Pfam family pfam01258 the
FT                   C4-type zinc finger protein, DksA/TraR family, but only one
FT                   of the four key Cys residues is conserved. All members of
FT                   this protein family share an additional C-terminal domain.
FT                   Smaller proteins from the proteobacteria with just the
FT                   N-terminal domain, including DksA and DksA2 are RNA
FT                   polymerase-binding regulatory proteins even if the
FT                   Zn-binding site is not conserved. [Unknown function,
FT                   General] [Superfamily, Aligned:6-69, Eval:3.9e-08,
FT                   score:43.5, N-term missing]"
