FT                   /note="Domain:cl27212:GlnS Glutamyl- or glutaminyl-tRNA
FT                   synthetase [Translation, ribosomal structure and
FT                   biogenesis]. The glutamyl-tRNA synthetases of the
FT                   eukaryotic cytosol and of the Archaea are more similar to
FT                   glutaminyl-tRNA synthetases than to bacterial glutamyl-tRNA
FT                   synthetases. This model models just the bacterial and
FT                   mitochondrial forms of the enzyme. In many species, the
FT                   charging of tRNA(gln) proceeds first through misacylation
FT                   with Glu and then transamidation. For this reason,
FT                   glutamyl-tRNA synthetases may act on both tRNA(gln) and
FT                   tRNA(glu). This model is highly specific. Proteins with
FT                   positive scores below the trusted cutoff may be fragments
FT                   rather than full-length sequences. [Protein synthesis, tRNA
FT                   aminoacylation] [Superfamily, Aligned:1-232, Eval:1.8e-94,
FT                   score:284.6, C-term missing]"
