FT                   /note="Domain:cl27057:ADK Adenylate kinase. Comparisons of
FT                   adenylate kinases have revealed a particular divergence in
FT                   the active site lid. In some organisms, particularly the
FT                   Gram-positive bacteria, residues in the lid domain have
FT                   been mutated to cysteines and these cysteine residues are
FT                   responsible for the binding of a zinc ion. The bound zinc
FT                   ion in the lid domain, is clearly structurally homologous
FT                   to Zinc-finger domains. However, it is unclear whether the
FT                   adenylate kinase lid is a novel zinc-finger DNA/RNA binding
FT                   domain, or that the lid bound zinc serves a purely
FT                   structural function. [Superfamily, Aligned:1-176,
FT                   Eval:4.8e-12, score:58.4]"
